description:
In the coalescing task (events.rs lines 355-360), when a batch is entirely type-filtered and close_after_first is true:

  if live_tx.send(None).await {  // error discarded with let _ =
  }
  continue;

After sending None, the live_rx end has been dropped (the SSE stream terminated via take_while). Subsequent None sends return Err(SendError) which is discarded. The task loops back to rx.recv().await and will keep running indefinitely, discarding every subsequent broadcast event, until either:
(a) The broadcast channel closes (AppState dropped, i.e. daemon shuts down), or
(b) A non-empty (non-filtered) batch arrives, which triggers live_tx.send(Some(...)).await.is_err() == true and breaks.

In a typical deployment the broadcast channel lives for the daemon's entire lifetime, so case (a) is daemon shutdown. If the type filter is strict (e.g. types=Contact on a chat-only workload), case (b) never fires. The task persists for the session lifetime.

Fix: change 'let _ = live_tx.send(None).await' to check the return value and break if the channel is dead:
  if live_tx.send(None).await.is_err() { break; }
  continue;
